# Submitted league bots are hashed, not diffed (issue #32).
#
# `bot_sha256` is captured over the bot's ORIGINAL bytes at submit time and the provenance
# token is signed against that hash. `store.py` re-hashes the COMMITTED bytes at load time.
# If git rewrites line endings in transit the two disagree, store.py silently restamps
# bot_sha256, the provenance token stops binding, and `load_submissions()` raises
# ValueError -- failing the WHOLE league load, not just the offending row.
#
# A Windows contributor's default `core.autocrlf=true` performs exactly that rewrite at
# commit time, which is after submit.py's byte-preserving copy has already put the correct
# bytes on disk. Marking the path `-text` stops git translating newlines in either
# direction, so the committed blob is byte-identical to what was hashed.
league/submissions/**/main.py -text
